"""OpenTelemetry Astronomy Shop Demo manifest.

A polyglot microservice e-commerce demo illustrating OpenTelemetry
instrumentation across many languages and runtimes.

Architecture reference: https://opentelemetry.io/docs/demo/architecture/
Source: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-demo
"""

from scryr import Diagram, Info, Link, Manifest
from scryr.types import (
    Classification,
    DeploymentTarget,
    Markdown,
    MetricTool,
    ProgrammingLanguage,
    Url,
    WebFramework,
    parse_version,
)

_SOURCE = Url("https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-demo")
_DOCS = Url("https://opentelemetry.io/docs/demo/")
kafka_block = Manifest(
    name="Kafka",
    icon="📨",
    classification=Classification.queue,
    tags=["messaging", "async", "infra"],
    connections=[],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "### Order event backbone\n"
            "\n"
            "Apache Kafka message queue used for async order events between Checkout, Accounting, and Fraud Detection.\n"
            "\n"
            "#### What to inspect\n"
            "\n"
            "| Area | Investigation |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| **Producer acknowledgements** | Distinguish accepted events from timed-out publishing attempts |\n"
            "| **Consumer lag** | Compare Accounting and Fraud Detection independently |\n"
            "| **Retention** | Keep a replay window appropriate for the exercise |\n"
            "\n"
            "#### Illustrative flow\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "Checkout -> Kafka -> Accounting / Fraud Detection\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "#### Suggested demo exercise\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Establish a baseline.\n"
            "   - Pause one consumer while continuing checkout traffic. Compare the growing backlog with the unaffected consumer, then resume it and follow the catch-up period.\n"
            "2. Compare the evidence.\n"
            "   - Correlate **traces**, *logs*, and metrics within the same time window.\n"
            "   - Save the relevant trace ID with the observed result.\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Replay the same sample order twice and inspect downstream duplicate handling.\n"
            "- [ ] Restore the starting configuration after the exercise.\n"
            "\n"
            "> These are proposed learning exercises, not guarantees about configured alerts,\n"
            "> recovery policies, or production readiness.\n"
            "\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - No web framework is modeled for this component; inspect its service runtime and integration clients instead.\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - Maven or Gradle for builds\n"
            "  - JUnit for focused tests\n"
            "  - Java Flight Recorder for runtime investigation\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `loki`\n"
            "  - `jaeger`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=parse_version("3.6.0"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.java],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.k8s_cluster, DeploymentTarget.helm],
        owners="Platform",
        metric_tools=[
            MetricTool.prometheus,
            MetricTool.loki,
            MetricTool.jaeger,
            MetricTool.grafana,
        ],
        links=[Link(site_name="Demo Docs", http_url=_DOCS)],
    ),
)
valkey_block = Manifest(
    name="Valkey",
    icon="🗄️",
    classification=Classification.cache_store,
    tags=["cache", "infra"],
    connections=[],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "### Session cart storage\n"
            "\n"
            "Valkey (Redis-compatible) in-memory cache used by the Cart Service to store shopping cart state.\n"
            "\n"
            "#### What to inspect\n"
            "\n"
            "| Area | Investigation |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| **Memory usage** | Compare cart growth with eviction pressure |\n"
            "| **Command latency** | Separate storage time from Cart request time |\n"
            "| **Missing key** | Distinguish an empty cart from a storage outage |\n"
            "\n"
            "#### Illustrative flow\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "Cart -> Valkey -> cart contents\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "#### Suggested demo exercise\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Establish a baseline.\n"
            "   - Add items to two independent sessions and confirm that their carts remain separate. Restart the cache in a disposable environment and observe how the storefront handles missing state.\n"
            "2. Compare the evidence.\n"
            "   - Correlate **traces**, *logs*, and metrics within the same time window.\n"
            "   - Save the relevant trace ID with the observed result.\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Record the intended cart lifetime and recovery behavior before choosing persistence settings.\n"
            "- [ ] Restore the starting configuration after the exercise.\n"
            "\n"
            "> These are proposed learning exercises, not guarantees about configured alerts,\n"
            "> recovery policies, or production readiness.\n"
            "\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - No web framework is modeled for this component; inspect its service runtime and integration clients instead.\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - Container logs for process diagnostics\n"
            "  - Resource metrics for capacity review\n"
            "  - Versioned configuration for repeatable environments\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `loki`\n"
            "  - `jaeger`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=parse_version("7.2.0"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.c],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.k8s_cluster, DeploymentTarget.helm],
        owners="Platform",
        metric_tools=[
            MetricTool.prometheus,
            MetricTool.loki,
            MetricTool.jaeger,
            MetricTool.grafana,
        ],
        links=[Link(site_name="Demo Docs", http_url=_DOCS)],
    ),
)
